TITLE:: MaplinMatrix
summary:: Stereo-to-Quad Matrix Processor
categories:: UGens>Multichannel
related:: Classes/FoaEncoderMatrix, Classes/Balance2

DESCRIPTION::
MaplinMatrix converts stereo input to a 4-channel quad output using matrix processing. The algorithm is based on the Maplin SM-333 hardware unit circuit analysis.

Processing includes:
- Sum/difference matrix
- Multi-stage allpass filtering
- Frequency-dependent delays
- BBD (Bucket Brigade Device) emulation
- Thermal noise and saturation modeling

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
Converts stereo input to quad output.

ARGUMENT:: leftIn
Left channel audio input.

ARGUMENT:: rightIn  
Right channel audio input.

ARGUMENT:: surroundLevel
Rear channel level (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.8).

ARGUMENT:: effectLevel
Matrix effect intensity (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.8).

ARGUMENT:: delayTime
Delay time control (0.0 to 1.0, maps to 5-50ms, default 0.4).

ARGUMENT:: active
Processing bypass (0 = bypass, 1 = active, default 1).
When bypassed, returns [leftIn, rightIn, 0, 0].

returns:: Array of 4 channels [frontLeft, frontRight, rearLeft, rearRight].

METHOD:: gui
Opens a control interface for MaplinMatrix parameters. Does not create audio processing - you must create your own synth.

ARGUMENT:: synth
The synth to control (optional). Must have surroundLevel, effectLevel, delayTime, and active parameters.

returns:: The GUI window for external control.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Basic stereo to quad conversion
(
{
    var stereo, quad;
    stereo = [SinOsc.ar(440), SinOsc.ar(880)] * 0.3;
    quad = MaplinMatrix.ar(stereo[0], stereo[1]);
    quad; // 4 channels out
}.play;
)

// With parameter control
(
var synth = {
    var input = [SinOsc.ar(440), SinOsc.ar(880)] * 0.3;
    MaplinMatrix.ar(
        leftIn: input[0],
        rightIn: input[1],
        surroundLevel: \surroundLevel.kr(0.8),
        effectLevel: \effectLevel.kr(0.8), 
        delayTime: \delayTime.kr(0.4),
        active: \active.kr(1)
    );
}.play;

// Parameter changes
synth.set(\surroundLevel, 1.0);
synth.set(\effectLevel, 0.5);
synth.set(\active, 0); // bypass
)

// Encoding to B-format
(
{
    var stereo, quad, bFormat;
    stereo = [SinOsc.ar(440), SinOsc.ar(880)] * 0.3;
    quad = MaplinMatrix.ar(stereo[0], stereo[1]);
    bFormat = FoaEncode.ar(quad, FoaEncoderMatrix.newQuad);
    FoaDecode.ar(bFormat, FoaDecoderKernel.newListen(1053));
}.play;
)

// GUI with user-created synth
(
// Create your own synth
var synth = {
    var input, output;
    input = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);
    output = MaplinMatrix.ar(input[0], input[1], 
        surroundLevel: \surroundLevel.kr(0.8),
        effectLevel: \effectLevel.kr(0.8),
        delayTime: \delayTime.kr(0.4),
        active: \active.kr(1)
    );
    Out.ar(0, output);
}.play;

// Open GUI to control the synth
var gui = MaplinMatrix.gui(synth);
)

// GUI without synth (controls only)
(
var gui = MaplinMatrix.gui();  // No synth - just interface
)

// GUI with metering (requires OSC messages from synth)
(
var synth = {
    var input, output;
    input = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);
    output = MaplinMatrix.ar(input[0], input[1], 
        surroundLevel: \surroundLevel.kr(0.8),
        effectLevel: \effectLevel.kr(0.8),
        delayTime: \delayTime.kr(0.4),
        active: \active.kr(1)
    );
    
    // Send meter data to GUI (optional)
    SendReply.kr(Impulse.kr(30), '/inputMeter', [
        Amplitude.kr(input[0]), Amplitude.kr(input[1])
    ]);
    SendReply.kr(Impulse.kr(30), '/outputMeter', [
        Amplitude.kr(output[0]), Amplitude.kr(output[1]), 
        Amplitude.kr(output[2]), Amplitude.kr(output[3])
    ]);
    
    Out.ar(0, output);
}.play;

var gui = MaplinMatrix.gui(synth);
)
::

SECTION:: Technical Details

The matrix processing implements:

LIST::
## Sum/difference extraction from stereo input
## Phase shifting using cascaded allpass filters
## Frequency band splitting (low/mid/high)
## Per-band delay processing
## BBD noise and bandwidth limiting
## Output scaling and saturation
::

Parameter ranges:
- surroundLevel: 0.0 = no rear output, 1.0 = rear matches front level
- effectLevel: 0.0 = minimal processing, 1.0 = full matrix effect
- delayTime: 0.0 = 5ms delay, 1.0 = 50ms delay
- active: 0 = bypass (stereo + silence), 1 = process 